2102 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 124 0 R
/E (Avenue Supermarts exhibits a robust financial profile, characterized by an impressive Interest Coverage Ratio that peaked at 58.19 in 2024 before settling at 52.52 in 2025. This significantly outperforms peers like Reliance Retail and V-Mart, underscoring DMart's minimal reliance on debt and its immense capacity to service financial obligations.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [147]
>>
endobj
2103 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 124 0 R
/E (The company's return ratios, while healthy, have seen a slight moderation with Return on Equity \(ROE\) at 12.63% and Return on Capital Employed \(ROCE\) at 16.39% for March 2025. While Reliance Retail currently leads in ROCE, DMart remains a top-tier performer, maintaining consistent profitability across its aggressive expansion phases.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [148]
>>
endobj
2104 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 124 0 R
/E (Valuation metrics indicate a cooling trend, with the Price-to-Earnings \(P/E\) ratio dropping from a high of 174 in 2022 to 98 in 2025. This suggests a shift toward more sustainable market pricing even as the company maintains a stable EBITDA margin of 8%, proving its operational resilience in a competitive retail landscape.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [149]
>>
endobj
